---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { OPERATOR, TAKEDOWN_EMAIL } from '../data/site.js';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy · beforegta6.wtf"
  description="What beforegta6.wtf collects about visitors, and what it does not."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
    <p>
      beforegta6.wtf is a hobby site by {OPERATOR}, Belgium. Questions or requests: the{' '}
      <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> or{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${TAKEDOWN_EMAIL}`}>{TAKEDOWN_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>What this site collects</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>There are no accounts. This site sets no cookies of its own.</li>
      <li>
        Cloudflare delivers the site. It processes your IP address to do that and to block attacks (
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">
          Cloudflare privacy policy
        </a>
        ).
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Page views (Umami)</h2>
    <p>
      Umami counts page views and page load times. It runs on our own server. For each page view it
      records:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>the page address and title, and the address of the site that sent you</li>
      <li>your browser, operating system, device type, screen size and language</li>
      <li>your country, region and city, which Umami finds from your IP address</li>
      <li>how fast the page loads (TTFB, FCP, LCP, CLS and INP), and how long it was open</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Umami uses no cookies and does not store your IP address. It does not record your screen or
      where you click. It groups page views into visits with a code made from your IP address and
      your browser. That code is pseudonymous, not anonymous, so the law treats it as personal data.
    </p>
    <p>
      Legal basis: our legitimate interest in knowing which pages people read and whether the site
      is fast (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)). We keep the records until we delete them. There is no automatic
      deletion yet.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can object at any time. This button stops Umami from counting your visits in this browser.
      The choice is stored in this browser only.
    </p>
    <p class="optout">
      <button id="optout" type="button" hidden>
        Stop counting my visits
      </button>
      <span role="status"></span>
    </p>
    <h2 id="contact-form">Contact form</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> sends your e-mail address, the subject, the link and
      your message to Formspark (Trampoline Software SRL, Belgium). Formspark stores them in Ireland
      and Germany and e-mails them to us. Formspark also receives your IP address and data about
      your browser when you send the form (
      <a href="https://formspark.io/legal/privacy-policy/" rel="noopener">
        Formspark privacy policy
      </a>
      ).
    </p>
    <p>
      When you open the contact page, Cloudflare Turnstile checks that you are a person, not a bot.
      To do that, it processes your IP address and data about your browser. Legal basis: our
      legitimate interest in keeping spam out (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)) (
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/" rel="noopener">
        Turnstile privacy addendum
      </a>
      ).
    </p>
    <p>
      We use a message only to answer it and to act on it. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in
      answering the messages people send (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)). We keep messages until we delete them.
    </p>
    <h2>Ads</h2>
    <p>
      Google AdSense shows the ads on this site. Google and its partners use cookies, similar
      identifiers and your IP address to show ads, to measure them and to stop fraud. Google can use
      your visits to this site and to other sites to choose the ads you see.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Visitors from the EEA, the UK and Switzerland first see Google's consent message. There you
        choose if Google may use your data for personalised ads.
      </li>
      <li>
        Turn off personalised ads from Google:{' '}
        <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">
          Google's ad settings
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        Turn off personalised ads from other ad companies:{' '}
        <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu" rel="noopener">
          youronlinechoices.eu
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">
          How Google uses data from sites that show its ads
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Links</h2>
    <p>
      Every card links to a post on another site, such as Reddit, X, YouTube or TikTok. Those sites
      have their own privacy policies.
    </p>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under the GDPR you can ask what we hold about you, and ask us to delete it. You can also
      complain to the Belgian Data Protection Authority (
      <a href="https://www.dataprotectionauthority.be" rel="noopener">
        dataprotectionauthority.be
      </a>
      ).
    </p>
    <p>
      <small>
        Last updated: <time datetime="2026-11-17">17 November 2026</time>.
      </small>
    </p>
  </article>
  <script>
    import '../scripts/optout.js';
  </script>
</Base>
